<div class="note small"><strong>Drawer / mixed stack syntax:</strong> <strong><code>O</code> means the LETTER O ("oh") for Open — not the digit zero (<code>0</code>).</strong> For example, <code>D7, O9.5, D7</code> means drawer, open cubby, drawer. You may write <code>Open 9.5</code> instead of <code>O9.5</code> if that is clearer. An all-number list such as <code>7, 7, 9.5</code> remains legacy all-drawer mode. Once you use <code>D</code> to mark drawers, any bare number is also interpreted as an open cubby: <code>D9, D9, 15</code> means two 9-unit drawers with a 15-unit clear cubby above. <strong>Open-shelf cabinets:</strong> use the same field for clear opening heights, bottom to top, for example <code>9.5, 12, auto</code>. Each boundary between openings gets an adjustable pin-supported shelf; <code>auto</code> is allowed only for the final/top opening and uses the remaining clear height. If the field is blank, the Shelves count still creates evenly spaced adjustable shelves. Values use the selected unit; explicit <code>mm</code> or <code>in</code> suffixes are also accepted.</div></section>

<section class="card"><h2>Drawer sizing</h2><div class="grid">
<div><label>Drawer depth</label><input id="drawerDepth" type="number" step="0.125"><div class="hint">24&quot; for your 24&quot; slides.</div></div>
<div><label>Total slide clearance</label><input id="slideClearance" type="number" step="0.03125"><div class="hint">Default 1&quot; total = 1/2&quot; each side.</div></div>
<div><label>Drawer side/front/back thickness</label><input id="drawerSidePly" type="number" step="0.125"><div class="hint">Default 1/2&quot; birch.</div></div>
<div><label>Drawer bottom thickness</label><input id="drawerBottomPly" type="number" step="0.125"><div class="hint">Default 1/2&quot; birch; panel fits completely between the four drawer walls.</div></div>
<div><label>Gap between drawer boxes</label><input id="drawerBoxGap" type="number" min="0" step="0.03125"><div class="hint">Default 1/2&quot;. This is a design choice, not a slide standard.</div></div>
<div><label>Bottom drawer-box clearance</label><input id="drawerBottomClearance" type="number" min="0" step="0.03125"><div class="hint">Default 1/2&quot; above the cabinet bottom. Drawer boxes are stacked upward from here.</div></div>
<div><label>Mixed-cabinet divider depth</label><input id="mixedPanelDepth" type="number" min="1" step="0.125"><div class="hint">Default 24&quot;. Horizontal panels that form the top/bottom of an open cubby.</div></div>
<div><label>Mixed-cabinet divider material</label><select id="mixedPanelMaterial"><option value="cherry">3/4&quot; cherry</option><option value="birch">3/4&quot; birch</option></select><div class="hint">Default cherry. Any drawer cabinet containing an open cubby now uses a cherry carcass so the exposed interior is cherry.</div></div>
</div>
<div class="note small"><strong>Width rule:</strong> drawer box outside width = cabinet inside width − total slide clearance. <strong>Height rule:</strong> drawer boxes must fit between the top of the 3/4&quot; cabinet bottom and the underside of the 3/4&quot; top stretchers, so the default 38&quot; carcass has 36.5&quot; of internal vertical drawer-box space. Vertical drawer spacing is <em>not</em> standardized by the slides. Drawer boxes and open cubbies are stacked from the bottom upward. Open-cubby heights are clear opening heights; 3/4&quot; divider panels are added where required. A top open cubby is anchored to the underside of the top stretchers so its entered clear height is exact. Verify your slide manufacturer's horizontal clearance before cutting.</div></section>

<section class="card"><h2>Face-frame options</h2><div class="grid">
<div><label>Face-frame stile width</label><input id="frameStileWidth" type="number" min="0.25" step="0.125"><div class="hint">Default 1 1/2&quot;. Full-height left/right members.</div></div>
<div><label>Face-frame rail width</label><input id="frameRailWidth" type="number" min="0.25" step="0.125"><div class="hint">Default 1 1/2&quot;. Top and bottom perimeter rails.</div></div>
<div><label>Face-frame thickness</label><input id="frameThickness" type="number" min="0.25" step="0.125"><div class="hint">Default 3/4&quot;. Frame is applied to the front of the carcass.</div></div>
<div><label>Face-frame material</label><select id="frameMaterial"><option value="cherry">Cherry solid stock</option><option value="birch">Birch solid stock</option></select><div class="hint">Face-frame members are treated as linear solid-wood stock, not plywood-sheet parts.</div></div>
<div><label>Overlay beyond frame opening</label><input id="frameOverlay" type="number" min="0" step="0.03125"><div class="hint">Default 1/2&quot; per edge for face-frame overlay fronts.</div></div>
<div><label>Inset reveal per edge</label><input id="frameInsetReveal" type="number" min="0" step="0.03125"><div class="hint">Default 1/16&quot; around inset doors/fronts.</div></div>
</div><div class="note small"><strong>Version 1.1 face frames are perimeter frames:</strong> two full-height stiles plus a top and bottom rail. CabinetDrafter does not yet generate intermediate face-frame rails between individual drawers or cubbies. Overlay and inset front sizing is calculated against the perimeter frame opening.</div></section>

